kawaranai hazu wa nai yo te wo nobashite

02:41.020 --> 02:42.890
Everything will change if you just reach out

02:50.580 --> 02:55.820
THREE NOCTURNAL CREATURES

02:51.330 --> 02:54.040
This looks more like a hospital than a school.

02:54.250 --> 02:55.670
It's private tutoring.

02:55.840 --> 03:01.430
80 PEOPLE HAVE BEEN ACCEPTED INTO REPUTABLE COLLEGES!

02:56.000 --> 02:57.210
Every day?

02:57.380 --> 03:00.090
Of course not. It's way too expensive.

03:01.590 --> 03:05.430
ADMISSION FORM

03:01.630 --> 03:05.430
I just have to study hard to get into a good college.

03:05.720 --> 03:07.310
Do you want to go to college?

03:07.520 --> 03:10.190
To tell you the truth, no, not really.

03:10.480 --> 03:13.560
Problem is, the world ain't too kind without a college degree.

03:13.770 --> 03:15.860
Yeah, you've got a point there.

03:16.020 --> 03:18.320
And people love to give you a hard time.

03:18.990 --> 03:21.860
Anyway, that's your business, not mine.

03:22.030 --> 03:24.570
As long as you have time to rehearse.

03:25.620 --> 03:28.830
You're free in the evenings and at weekends, aren't you?

03:29.040 --> 03:31.370
Then there's the question of work.

03:31.920 --> 03:33.290
Just a minute.

03:37.300 --> 03:38.170
A band?

03:38.340 --> 03:40.340
- You were up for it.
- I didn't say I was.

03:40.670 --> 03:41.550
Yes, you did.

03:41.720 --> 03:44.340
You asked me to keep my middle finger straight.

03:44.510 --> 03:47.680
Just don't whip it out like that, okay?

03:47.850 --> 03:48.850
Ouch.

03:49.100 --> 03:51.480
Besides, I never said anything about singing.

03:51.640 --> 03:53.480
To each her own.

03:53.850 --> 03:57.110
Me with school, you with music.

03:57.360 --> 03:59.030
Oh yeah, nothing to do with that.

03:59.400 --> 04:01.860
I didn't think it made much sense.

04:02.200 --> 04:04.660
You weren't the only one surprised.

04:06.410 --> 04:09.120
It's crazy, the train being packed so early.

04:09.870 --> 04:11.290
Check out the country girl.

04:11.580 --> 04:12.500
Shut up.

04:12.960 --> 04:16.330
Well, I'm sure you'll find some time for music,

04:17.210 --> 04:19.130
no matter how hard you work, right?

04:19.420 --> 04:21.260
You're way too optimistic.

04:21.550 --> 04:23.760
I'm not talking about learning an instrument.

04:24.090 --> 04:27.510
If you ask me, you'd make a great singer.

04:27.760 --> 04:29.310
Me, a singer?

04:29.760 --> 04:32.600
I swear, you've got the voice and the charisma.

04:33.060 --> 04:34.310
Who, me?

04:34.480 --> 04:35.150
You do.

04:35.480 --> 04:36.650
You know, a band

04:37.110 --> 04:41.570
a band brings together people who have a lot on their minds.

04:42.650 --> 04:45.030
Who want to shout "I want to find love",

04:45.280 --> 04:47.780
"The world is rotten",

04:48.200 --> 04:50.870
"I'm completely overwhelmed",

04:51.330 --> 04:54.620
"I love myself", or "I hate myself".

04:56.580 --> 04:58.920
I thought you wanted to sing solo.

04:59.590 --> 05:03.760
I thought so too, but I miss being in a band.

05:04.380 --> 05:08.300
It turns into a viper's nest. A little thing takes on enormous proportions,

05:08.470 --> 05:12.720
to the point where you end up resenting everyone.

05:13.020 --> 05:16.020
And boom, you keep everything to yourself and you explode.

05:16.190 --> 05:17.810
There's absolutely nothing positive about it.

05:18.610 --> 05:19.980
Oh, yeah, that's true.

05:20.610 --> 05:22.480
But a band is fun.

05:22.650 --> 05:27.070
It's giving life to something you couldn't create on your own.

05:28.530 --> 05:29.160
What's that?

05:29.320 --> 05:30.740
Nothing at all.

05:32.040 --> 05:35.370
It's this station, the one closest to your house.

05:35.910 --> 05:39.210
You'd think we were out of town like this.

05:39.540 --> 05:41.340
Well, it's not that bad.

05:41.500 --> 05:43.000
Over there's your studio.

05:43.170 --> 05:45.300
There's a supermarket nearby.

05:45.470 --> 05:46.680
Is there? Noted.

05:46.930 --> 05:47.430
Ouch.

05:50.010 --> 05:51.350
Are you sure about this?

05:51.680 --> 05:52.470
Of course I'm sure.

05:52.930 --> 05:55.350
This is for housing me.

05:55.810 --> 05:57.480
- Anyway...
- No worries.

05:57.730 --> 05:59.980
Can you put the rest in the fridge?

06:00.230 --> 06:02.770
Well, I'll warn you, I'm not much of a chef.

06:02.940 --> 06:05.030
Maybe, but you can cook.

06:05.190 --> 06:06.650
Let's just say I don't hate it.

06:06.820 --> 06:09.360
Well, let's see... a knife.

06:10.620 --> 06:13.620
It's a bit like composing a song, if you like.

06:13.950 --> 06:16.450
You chop the vegetables while the water boils.

06:16.620 --> 06:19.750
You prepare the sauce and let it simmer.

06:19.920 --> 06:21.670
You juggle a lot of things,

06:21.840 --> 06:25.460
before bringing it all together to form a cohesive whole.

06:26.510 --> 06:27.970
It doesn't cut a thing!

06:28.130 --> 06:30.640
Sorry, I don't have another one.

06:30.930 --> 06:32.890
You don't have to apologize.

06:33.220 --> 06:36.730
This is the kind of detail that reminds me that I'm a liability.

06:37.100 --> 06:38.890
I'll never make it on my own.

06:40.270 --> 06:41.560
Do you think I'm stupid?

06:41.730 --> 06:43.900
Not at all. I used to be like you.

06:45.280 --> 06:48.110
The best thing you can do is just take the plunge.

06:48.490 --> 06:51.160
You have to fumble your way to success.

06:51.320 --> 06:53.410
<i>Flip 'em off!</i>

06:51.780 --> 06:54.200
We all learn from our mistakes.

06:55.330 --> 06:57.330
Like learning how to buy a plate.

06:57.870 --> 06:58.750
Sorry.

06:59.580 --> 07:01.420
<i>To buy: plates, ladles, rods, strainers</i>

06:59.870 --> 07:01.420
And that's the job.

07:02.750 --> 07:04.670
We're going to have to put up lights, too.

07:05.050 --> 07:07.420
Wait, are we going to eat with this?

07:08.050 --> 07:11.090
Say, aren't we a little spoiled around here?

07:11.550 --> 07:13.550
That's a bourgeois remark.

07:14.300 --> 07:17.850
Well, you're not at all.
I come from an ordinary family.

07:18.770 --> 07:21.440
Ordinary... with a few quirks.

07:21.900 --> 07:23.810
We have a lot of rules.

07:24.060 --> 07:24.860
Rules?

07:25.980 --> 07:27.820
Like, in the family circle?

07:28.400 --> 07:29.150
Well, yeah.

07:30.490 --> 07:34.910
Number one, always share dinner with the rest of the family.

07:35.120 --> 07:39.450
<i>Family precepts</i>

07:35.740 --> 07:39.450
Second, no cell phones in the living room.

07:40.500 --> 07:44.790
Third, mandatory family reunion every Sunday night.

07:45.460 --> 07:46.170
Among other things.

07:47.590 --> 07:48.250
How annoying.

07:48.550 --> 07:53.220
My parents took great pride in bossing us around.

07:53.430 --> 07:55.390
Eventually, word got out at school.

07:55.550 --> 07:58.100
Yeah, it's not that surprising.

07:58.520 --> 08:03.270
One day, I stopped going to class, and dropped out of high school shortly afterwards.

08:03.440 --> 08:04.350
Why would you do that?

08:04.650 --> 08:07.110
It's not that big a deal.

08:10.860 --> 08:11.610
I know it isn't.

08:11.950 --> 08:13.450
And how do you know?

08:14.240 --> 08:15.530
I can see it in your eyes.

08:17.740 --> 08:20.250
Pretty girl, most popular girl in school...

08:20.580 --> 08:23.160
She had all the boys over her.

08:23.540 --> 08:26.380
And what, she took a dislike to you?

08:26.710 --> 08:27.420
Yeah, she did.

08:27.960 --> 08:28.840
Why would she do that?

08:29.460 --> 08:30.800
That's a good question.

08:31.170 --> 08:33.430
Maybe she didn't like the way I looked.

08:33.590 --> 08:35.300
And you didn't force yourself on her?

08:35.680 --> 08:36.760
That kind of girl

08:36.930 --> 08:40.850
puts everyone in her pocket before showing her true face.

08:41.560 --> 08:44.600
She'd even send her friends after me.

08:44.890 --> 08:47.230
I ended up in hospital once,

08:47.400 --> 08:50.900
but even my parents asked me to take it easy.

08:51.070 --> 08:51.860
Stop.

08:52.400 --> 08:54.740
Eat before it overcooks.

08:55.110 --> 08:57.660
Don't worry, I like my vegetables well done.

08:58.740 --> 09:01.410
You see, you're cut out for singing.

09:02.040 --> 09:04.960
Everything you've told me... That's like five songs.

09:05.290 --> 09:09.710
I'd like to be in a band where I don't have to be the singer.

09:09.920 --> 09:12.960
I'd like to be able to concentrate on the guitar.

09:13.510 --> 09:14.590
For real?

09:14.920 --> 09:15.880
Well, yeah.

09:20.140 --> 09:21.970
<i>Dropping out of high school</i>

09:22.270 --> 09:25.480
<i>is like throwing away your future.</i>

09:25.940 --> 09:29.440
<i>There's no going back, even if you change your mind.</i>

09:31.230 --> 09:31.980
<i>In that case...</i>

09:32.230 --> 09:34.610
<i>do I need to secure a place at college?</i>

09:34.780 --> 09:37.200
<i>If that's the case, I'll study in my corner.</i>

09:38.570 --> 09:41.370
No, if I stay out of school

09:41.530 --> 09:44.040
and without a degree, I'm screwed for good.

09:44.910 --> 09:45.660
Ruined, eh?

09:45.910 --> 09:48.630
No, you know what I mean.

09:48.920 --> 09:53.090
It's just that giving up on this project means admitting defeat.

09:53.630 --> 09:56.930
I can't fold like I did before.

09:58.180 --> 09:59.010
I hear you.

09:59.590 --> 10:01.140
I'll leave you alone.

10:02.100 --> 10:03.060
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

10:03.720 --> 10:05.600
Stop apologizing, I said.

10:06.310 --> 10:08.440
I think there's some beer left.

10:14.730 --> 10:15.490
It's heavy!

10:15.990 --> 10:17.740
Of course, they're books.

10:17.900 --> 10:20.620
I'll do the big ones, you do the rest.

10:21.120 --> 10:23.950
I'll manage. Are you going to be all right in one trip?

10:24.200 --> 10:26.620
Yeah, that was the big one.

10:26.960 --> 10:28.750
Can you check your room?

10:28.920 --> 10:29.580
Yeah, right away.

10:32.590 --> 10:33.920
She took everything.

10:35.920 --> 10:37.590
And now, let's get to work.

10:41.640 --> 10:42.220
There you go.

10:42.510 --> 10:44.260
You're going to need this.

10:44.510 --> 10:46.390
Yeah, that's good.

10:47.020 --> 10:50.270
Anyway, I don't know how to play it.

10:53.190 --> 10:55.780
You're not wrong, I'd better get it back.

10:58.070 --> 10:58.990
Thanks for the offer.

11:01.030 --> 11:01.910
Well, I'm off.

11:02.740 --> 11:05.790
- You don't need me to come with you?
- That'll do.

11:06.450 --> 11:07.160
If you say so.

11:09.210 --> 11:12.670
If you don't mind, can I ask you one last favor?

11:12.880 --> 11:13.920
Name it.

11:19.630 --> 11:21.550
I've never been here before.

11:21.930 --> 11:24.300
It's the Tama River. You know it?

11:24.720 --> 11:26.390
Well, it's really big.

11:26.680 --> 11:29.060
I didn't know there was so much nature in Tokyo.

11:29.850 --> 11:31.560
Tokyo is on the other side of that bridge.

11:31.900 --> 11:32.980
That's a shame.

11:33.230 --> 11:35.150
We're right on the edge.

11:36.570 --> 11:38.570
How about that favor?

11:38.820 --> 11:39.990
Pick a song.

11:40.240 --> 11:43.570
I want to hear you sing something one last time.

11:43.950 --> 11:45.370
Any song you like.

11:46.410 --> 11:49.000
And good luck with your classes.

11:49.370 --> 11:52.580
I'm moving back in with my roommate, by the way.

11:52.830 --> 11:55.590
We should get together again sometime.

11:56.670 --> 11:57.300
Definitely.

11:57.500 --> 12:00.340
I hope it works out for you too.

12:03.800 --> 12:07.220
I promise I'll compose something you'll like.

12:07.600 --> 12:08.180
Sounds great.

12:08.520 --> 12:10.730
Prove your critics wrong, middle finger out.

12:11.270 --> 12:12.230
Do the same.

12:13.810 --> 12:14.480
Now, hold on.

12:15.770 --> 12:18.860
If you can hold out your pinkie instead of your middle finger...

12:19.940 --> 12:21.240
I'll do it, too.

12:22.490 --> 12:23.280
That's a promise.

12:31.200 --> 12:31.830
Here goes.

12:34.170 --> 12:40.300
<i>How can we hope to move forward?</i>

12:41.840 --> 12:44.720
<i>Everything's so white
Everything's so slow</i>

12:45.090 --> 12:50.220
<i>All answers are empty of substance</i>

12:50.390 --> 12:54.730
<i>My fingers are static
My fingers are trembling</i>

12:54.890 --> 12:57.940
<i>There's no written answer
No stinging failure</i>

12:58.110 --> 13:03.190
<i>I've always been who I am
And I'll always be who I was</i>

13:03.360 --> 13:09.160
<i>No matter how hard I fight
There's no tomorrow</i>

13:16.080 --> 13:16.880
Damn.

13:20.210 --> 13:21.130
So...

13:22.800 --> 13:25.380
"Jim tells her not to give up.

13:25.550 --> 13:28.760
"A ray of hope always shines through..."

13:35.730 --> 13:37.060
I have a purchase to make.

13:38.770 --> 13:40.110
<i>Girls Band Cry.</i>

13:49.950 --> 13:54.290
And here's where it gets complicated. The right pronoun...

14:02.590 --> 14:04.090
It was a blast!

14:04.260 --> 14:06.260
I eliminated two people!

14:06.720 --> 14:08.510
- Classy!
- Yeah, I'm proud!

14:14.430 --> 14:15.930
I didn't talk to anyone.

14:19.020 --> 14:22.610
I haven't talked to anyone all week.

14:23.610 --> 14:25.190
<i>Can you see the end of the boxes?</i>

14:25.360 --> 14:27.700
<i>Yeah, I can. My back is killing me.</i>

14:27.860 --> 14:29.610
<i>Just try to get some rest.</i>

14:29.950 --> 14:30.700
<i>I appreciate that.</i>

14:33.660 --> 14:34.330
WOULD YOU LIKE TO...

14:37.370 --> 14:38.710
NEW MESSAGE

14:39.790 --> 14:41.630
Here we go again.

14:43.880 --> 14:44.460
NEW MESSAGE FROM MOMOKA

14:45.130 --> 14:49.010
<i>Did you buy a lamp? Just in case, I've got one to spare.</i>

14:50.180 --> 14:52.100
<i>Ah, I'd love to, thanks!</i>

14:54.720 --> 14:55.720
CAN I COME AND GET IT?

14:56.560 --> 14:57.560
Good evening.

14:57.810 --> 14:58.770
Ah, good evening.

15:02.900 --> 15:05.480
Normally, I wouldn't be too far away.

15:07.820 --> 15:08.900
This is it.

15:09.400 --> 15:10.780
This is it.

15:11.950 --> 15:13.620
Wow, that was fast.

15:13.990 --> 15:15.290
Careful, I'm coming in.

15:16.160 --> 15:18.120
Sorry to barge in on you like this.

15:18.290 --> 15:22.170
Look, I've put it here. Should do the trick, right?

15:22.670 --> 15:26.000
Oh, thank you so much. As long as it works, listen...

15:26.340 --> 15:28.130
So, how are we settling in?

15:28.630 --> 15:30.760
It's a little early to tell.

15:32.510 --> 15:34.930
Well, shall we grab a bite to eat?

15:35.100 --> 15:36.770
I'll pay, I've got a job.

15:38.270 --> 15:39.890
Oh, I'd love to.

15:40.940 --> 15:42.270
Is this your Nina?

15:43.360 --> 15:43.900
The famous one.

15:44.310 --> 15:45.770
This lamp was Awa's.

15:45.940 --> 15:48.030
My brand-new drummer.

15:48.490 --> 15:50.200
Hi, I'm Subaru Awa.

15:50.700 --> 15:51.610
How do you do?

15:52.780 --> 15:54.280
I'm Iseri.

15:54.450 --> 15:57.330
Would you like to join us?
But you have to pay your share.

15:57.490 --> 15:59.040
What's that? You skinflint.

15:59.290 --> 16:01.160
I'm not made of money.

16:01.870 --> 16:02.540
Shall we go?

16:05.040 --> 16:07.210
No, leave it, I'm going home.

16:07.380 --> 16:10.840
Come on, be nice. Nina just got here.

16:11.010 --> 16:13.050
Just think, Subaru is your age.

16:16.550 --> 16:18.560
Yeah, talk about shabu-shabu.

16:18.850 --> 16:20.520
You've added too many vegetables.

16:20.850 --> 16:25.310
Chinese cabbage loses all its flavor if you boil it too long.

16:25.650 --> 16:26.150
Here you go.

16:27.690 --> 16:28.400
Here you go.

16:28.650 --> 16:29.320
Thank you for this.

16:29.610 --> 16:32.700
So, tell me, what kind of music do you like?

16:33.530 --> 16:35.450
Do you have a favorite band or Vocaloid?

16:36.160 --> 16:39.660
She's more into classics, her grandmother was crazy about them.

16:40.750 --> 16:43.080
Ah, that's cool. I listen to those too.

16:43.250 --> 16:44.330
Who do you like?

16:44.870 --> 16:48.130
"Like" may be a big word...

16:48.290 --> 16:49.630
Am I dreaming or is it Glarech?

16:50.380 --> 16:51.260
That's a good point.

16:51.420 --> 16:53.260
So, you listen to them?

16:53.430 --> 16:56.590
Yeah, I've seen them twice, in concert and at a festival.

16:56.890 --> 17:00.100
- Like the one in Chiba?
- That's the one.

17:00.430 --> 17:02.350
Their performance sucked.

17:03.140 --> 17:04.480
Oh yeah?

17:04.890 --> 17:06.980
And since then, they've been producing nothing.

17:07.270 --> 17:10.030
Not one concert since that catastrophe.

17:10.190 --> 17:14.360
I didn't even notice, but now that you mention it...

17:14.650 --> 17:16.820
But the critics loved them.

17:17.280 --> 17:19.950
Have you ever played live, Nina?

17:20.330 --> 17:21.240
Not really, no.

17:21.410 --> 17:22.120
Bummer.

17:22.290 --> 17:24.540
Can I add the meat to the broth?

17:25.170 --> 17:26.170
Don't you like it?

17:26.580 --> 17:27.380
Nina?

17:29.000 --> 17:31.340
Sorry, I'll be right back.

17:37.390 --> 17:38.180
Don't you like her?

17:39.800 --> 17:40.560
No, I don't.

17:40.720 --> 17:42.810
Then talk to her.

17:42.970 --> 17:45.140
She's trying to make a move on you.

17:45.520 --> 17:47.400
Step towards me?

17:47.850 --> 17:50.400
What, she's forcing herself on me?

17:50.820 --> 17:53.030
It always takes effort at first.

17:53.190 --> 17:55.570
You don't know anything about each other.

17:56.200 --> 17:59.320
I don't know. I just... I feel like I'm being talked down to.

17:59.700 --> 18:01.120
You're imagining things.

18:01.280 --> 18:05.330
You know, she's an actress, it's part of her personality.

18:05.500 --> 18:07.040
She's not mean.

18:07.790 --> 18:09.210
Yeah, she's so generous!

18:09.540 --> 18:11.340
She is too kind

18:11.500 --> 18:15.300
to take an interest in a spoiled brat like me.

18:15.470 --> 18:16.800
You got a problem?

18:16.970 --> 18:18.050
I don't have a problem!

18:18.220 --> 18:22.430
You'll never make friends if you keep up that attitude.

18:28.440 --> 18:29.060
Get back here!

18:30.860 --> 18:31.650
You're right.

18:31.900 --> 18:35.190
I don't think I'll ever make any.

18:35.360 --> 18:36.780
I'm the problem.

18:37.030 --> 18:37.950
Okay, listen.

18:38.240 --> 18:40.530
I'm gonna be alone for the rest of my life.

18:41.240 --> 18:42.490
Thanks for the invitation.

18:47.910 --> 18:51.210
- Thanks for the lamp.
- It's nothing...

18:53.880 --> 18:55.710
She's so stubborn...

18:56.260 --> 18:58.550
She's already got everything she needs.

19:02.850 --> 19:04.350
What was I thinking?

19:13.900 --> 19:15.480
What was I doing?

19:16.190 --> 19:18.070
She was trying to be nice

19:18.740 --> 19:21.530
and get to know me, nothing more.

19:24.080 --> 19:25.290
I'm stupid.

19:27.410 --> 19:28.750
Too stupid.

19:30.620 --> 19:33.250
Totally stupid!

19:33.540 --> 19:36.880
A complete moron! A poor failure!

19:40.090 --> 19:41.380
An imbecile.

19:41.550 --> 19:42.720
Shut up, you!

19:42.890 --> 19:44.510
- You shut up!
- What did you say?

19:47.100 --> 19:48.390
Who do you think you are?

19:49.640 --> 19:51.770
Will you shut up?

19:52.690 --> 19:54.020
No, wait... stop!

19:54.730 --> 19:55.900
You shut up!

19:59.190 --> 20:01.530
You shut up!

20:31.060 --> 20:34.190
I can't even install a lamp on my own.

20:35.650 --> 20:37.610
I'll stay in the dark.

20:38.020 --> 20:41.150
I'm doomed to wander in the dark.

20:43.110 --> 20:44.320
In the darkness.

20:46.700 --> 20:49.080
Come on, let's form a band.

20:51.330 --> 20:52.330
Momoka?

20:52.830 --> 20:54.330
Subaru?

20:54.750 --> 20:57.130
You'd better hide your spare key.

20:57.340 --> 20:59.210
Besides, you broke the lamp.

21:03.380 --> 21:06.470
I already told you, but I love your voice.

21:07.050 --> 21:10.270
What do you gain by lying to me?

21:10.970 --> 21:12.100
I'm not lying.

21:12.350 --> 21:15.020
You're a paradox coupled with a ball of negativity.

21:15.190 --> 21:18.520
Precisely because you're incapable of lying to yourself.

21:18.900 --> 21:22.990
No matter how fragile you are, you refuse to let go.

21:24.700 --> 21:29.080
Like the old songs I buried deep in my memory.

21:29.330 --> 21:32.330
The ones I cherish the most and refuse

21:33.370 --> 21:34.370
to let go.

21:41.210 --> 21:45.380
You don't have to feel sorry for me...

21:51.470 --> 21:53.640
Stop laughing!

21:54.390 --> 21:55.390
What a pain!

21:57.480 --> 21:58.400
Ouch!

22:00.610 --> 22:03.900
Inject all your despair into your music.

22:04.740 --> 22:05.490
Into our music.

22:04.860 --> 22:05.900
DRINKING YOGHURT

22:06.070 --> 22:06.780
As a gift.

22:21.690 --> 22:24.440
Never influenced by anybody

22:27.720 --> 22:30.840
I laughed, thinking it a dream

22:30.840 --> 22:33.910
Numbed by the weakness I had forgotten

22:33.910 --> 22:37.110
I can't even say that I'm lonely

22:37.110 --> 22:39.850
This fragile heart

22:40.580 --> 22:45.980
Vulnerable to even casual conversation

22:46.930 --> 22:52.980
Is incapable of making anyone happy

22:52.980 --> 22:59.110
But still, I feel a growing hope

22:59.110 --> 23:02.330
Moving past all of the lies

23:02.330 --> 23:05.660
I just want to hear that I'm not wrong

23:05.660 --> 23:09.320
I'm a dreamer, I'm young

23:09.320 --> 23:11.810
I don't care if I'm still the same today

23:11.810 --> 23:15.280
I just want to sing with you

23:15.280 --> 23:18.250
My emotions stir so often

23:18.250 --> 23:21.690
I've been hated

23:21.690 --> 23:28.100
But I'm going to keep walking

23:28.100 --> 23:31.250
Proud of myself who can never become anybody

23:31.250 --> 23:34.550
Even if I'm alone

23:34.550 --> 23:41.900
I believe in myself

23:47.420 --> 23:49.380
<i>Next Episode: "Q&A without head or tail".</i>
